{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-02-Jul-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "On dividing a certain number by 304, we get 43 as the remainder. If the same number isdivided by 16, what will be the remainder?", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "The sum of the five consecutive even numbers is 2720. The sum of the third and fifth numbers is:", "options": [{"text": "1192", "added": false}, {"text": "1292", "added": false}, {"text": "1092", "added": false}, {"text": "1392", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "factors-divisors", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "An electric vehicle company produces three different car models: A, B and C. The production of three different models over a period of four years has been shown in the bar graph below. What is the difference between the average production of Model A in 2019, 2021 and 2022 and the average production of Model B in 2020, 2021 and 2022?", "options": [{"text": "95,000 cars", "added": false}, {"text": "80,000 cars", "added": false}, {"text": "45,000 cars", "added": false}, {"text": "50,000 cars", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Consider two concentric circles having radii 17 cm and 15 cm. What is the length (in cm) of the chord, of the bigger circle, which is a tangent to the smaller circle?", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "The volume of a cube is reduced to 72.9%. By how much is the side of the cube reduced?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "When a number is increased by 8, it becomes 120% of itself. The number is:", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "425", "added": false}, {"text": "444.5", "added": false}, {"text": "430.5", "added": false}, {"text": "440.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "47 masons can dig a 35 m long trench in one day. How many masons should be employed for digging a 105 m long trench of the same type in one day?", "options": [{"text": "94", "added": false}, {"text": "141", "added": false}, {"text": "128", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "efficiency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹1,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,050", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,250", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The distance between the centres of two circles of radii 4 cm and 2 cm is 10 cm. The length (in cm) of a transverse common tangent is:", "options": [{"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "If the brick size is 25 cm×12 cm×9 cm, then how many bricks are required to construct a wall of length 10 m, breadth 22.5 cm and height 6 m?", "options": [{"text": "6000", "added": false}, {"text": "4500", "added": false}, {"text": "5000", "added": false}, {"text": "8000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "29400", "added": false}, {"text": "23500", "added": false}, {"text": "19400", "added": false}, {"text": "27400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Two equal circles are drawn on a square in such a way that opposite side of the square forms the diameter of each circle. If the remaining area of the square is 42 cm2, what is the measurement (in cm) of the diameter of each circle?", "options": [{"text": "3.5", "added": false}, {"text": "2.5", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "From the salary of a software engineer, if 15% is used as house rent, 25% of the remaining is spent on household items, 25% of the remaining as income tax, and 15% of the remaining on clothing, then he is left with ₹10,404. Find his total salary.", "options": [{"text": "₹22,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹24,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹25,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹23,600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "If the side of a square is increased by 5%, then the percentage increase in its area will be:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "If 35 is the mean proportional of 25 and x, then what is value of x?", "options": [{"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "47", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "im